        "text": "The parametric ratio requires dx/dt ≠ 0 at the parameter value and an appropriate local inverse branch. In the example a ≠ 0 and t ≠ 0 are needed for the printed cancellation. If a = 0, the parametrization is a single point and the ratio is 0/0. For a ≠ 0 at t = 0, dx/dt = 0 but dy/dt ≠ 0, giving a vertical tangent; the displayed finite slope 1/t does not apply."
