        "type": "clarification",
        "text": "An implicit relation need not define one differentiable function y(x) everywhere. Differentiate along a differentiable branch, treating y as a function of x. For a smooth relation F(x,y) = 0, a nonzero F_y at a point gives a local differentiable y(x); then y′ = −F_x/F_y. If that denominator vanishes, the finite-slope formula cannot be used without examining the curve further."
