        "text": "The source does not specify branches for inverse secant and cosecant and selects a positive radical. Its formulas are valid on x > 1 under the standard branches. On the conventional arcsec range [0,π] excluding π/2 and arccsc range [−π/2,π/2] excluding 0, the formulas on both real intervals |x| > 1 are \\(\\frac{d}{dx}\\operatorname{arcsec}x=\\frac1{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\\) and \\(\\frac{d}{dx}\\operatorname{arccsc}x=\\frac{-1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\\). Their chain rules likewise use |u|. Neither has a finite derivative at |x| = 1. The arctan derivative holds for all real x; the decreasing arccot branch (0,π) gives −1/(1+x²) for all real x."
