        "text": "B.Taylor was a British mathematician who is known by his invention of Taylor’s theorem and the Taylor’s series. In 1708 he obtained the solution of the problem of the “centre of oscillation” and published on 1714. Calculus of finite differences add to the branch of higher mathematics in 1715 with the name “Methodus Incrementorum Directa et Inversa”. This word contain the well known layrange realized its importance and termed it as the main foundation of differential calculus."
