const math12Exercise52=[{"id": "ex-5-2-q1", "qNo": "1", "question": "Find the vector derivative: (a) \\(F⃗(t)=tî+t^2ĵ+(t+t^3)k̂\\); (b) \\(F⃗(s)=(sî+s^2ĵ+s^2k̂)+(2s^2î-sĵ+3k̂)\\); (c) \\(F⃗(\\theta)=\\cos\\theta[î+\\tan\\thetaĵ+3k̂]\\).", "steps": ["Differentiate each component with respect to its stated parameter.", "(a) The derivatives of t,t²,t+t³ are 1,2t,1+3t². Therefore F⃗′ = î+2tĵ+(1+3t²)k̂.", "(b) Combine the input vectors first: F⃗(s) = (s+2s²)î+(s²−s)ĵ+(s²+3)k̂.", "Differentiate: F⃗′(s) = (1+4s)î+(2s−1)ĵ+2sk̂.", "(c) On the original domain cos θ ≠ 0, expand to F⃗(θ) = cos θî+sin θĵ+3cos θk̂.", "Thus F⃗′(θ) = −sin θî+cos θĵ−3sin θk̂.", "The simplified formula extends across excluded points, but the printed tan θ expression and its derivative are defined only for cos θ ≠ 0."], "solution": "Differentiate each component with respect to its stated parameter.\n(a) The derivatives of t,t²,t+t³ are 1,2t,1+3t². Therefore F⃗′ = î+2tĵ+(1+3t²)k̂.\n(b) Combine the input vectors first: F⃗(s) = (s+2s²)î+(s²−s)ĵ+(s²+3)k̂.\nDifferentiate: F⃗′(s) = (1+4s)î+(2s−1)ĵ+2sk̂.\n(c) On the original domain cos θ ≠ 0, expand to F⃗(θ) = cos θî+sin θĵ+3cos θk̂.\nThus F⃗′(θ) = −sin θî+cos θĵ−3sin θk̂.\nThe simplified formula extends across excluded points, but the printed tan θ expression and its derivative are defined only for cos θ ≠ 0.", "answer": "(a) î+2tĵ+(1+3t²)k̂; (b) (1+4s)î+(2s−1)ĵ+2sk̂; (c) −sin θî+cos θĵ−3sin θk̂, cos θ ≠ 0.", "progressiveSolution": true, "solutionOrigin": "SpaceBook learning enhancement", "sourceReferences": [{"page": 139, "jpg": "074_page_1.jpg", "verification": "all source subparts and derivative orders checked at enlarged resolution"}]}, {"id": "ex-5-2-q2", "qNo": "2", "question": "Find second derivatives: (a) \\(t^2î+3t^3ĵ-8t^2k̂\\); (b) \\((3+s^2)î-(s+1)^2ĵ+3s^4k̂\\); (c) \\(\\ln xî-x^2k̂\\); (d) \\(\\sin^2\\thetaî-\\cos^2\\thetaĵ\\).", "steps": ["Take first derivatives, then differentiate again.", "(a) F⃗′ = 2tî+9t²ĵ−16tk̂; F⃗″ = 2î+18tĵ−16k̂.", "(b) F⃗′ = 2sî−2(s+1)ĵ+12s³k̂; F⃗″ = 2î−2ĵ+36s²k̂.", "(c) ln x requires x > 0. F⃗′ = x⁻¹î−2xk̂; F⃗″ = −x⁻²î−2k̂, on x > 0.", "(d) The derivative of sin²θ is 2sin θcos θ, and of −cos²θ is also 2sin θcos θ.", "Thus F⃗′(θ) = sin(2θ)(î+ĵ).", "Differentiate again: F⃗″(θ) = 2cos(2θ)(î+ĵ). All trigonometric derivatives use radians."], "solution": "Take first derivatives, then differentiate again.\n(a) F⃗′ = 2tî+9t²ĵ−16tk̂; F⃗″ = 2î+18tĵ−16k̂.\n(b) F⃗′ = 2sî−2(s+1)ĵ+12s³k̂; F⃗″ = 2î−2ĵ+36s²k̂.\n(c) ln x requires x > 0. F⃗′ = x⁻¹î−2xk̂; F⃗″ = −x⁻²î−2k̂, on x > 0.\n(d) The derivative of sin²θ is 2sin θcos θ, and of −cos²θ is also 2sin θcos θ.\nThus F⃗′(θ) = sin(2θ)(î+ĵ).\nDifferentiate again: F⃗″(θ) = 2cos(2θ)(î+ĵ). All trigonometric derivatives use radians.", "answer": "(a) 2î+18tĵ−16k̂; (b) 2î−2ĵ+36s²k̂; (c) −x⁻²î−2k̂, x > 0; (d) 2cos(2θ)(î+ĵ).", "progressiveSolution": true, "solutionOrigin": "SpaceBook learning enhancement", "sourceReferences": [{"page": 139, "jpg": "074_page_1.jpg", "verification": "all source subparts and derivative orders checked at enlarged resolution"}]}, {"id": "ex-5-2-q3", "qNo": "3", "question": "Differentiate the scalar functions: (a) \\(f(x)=[xî+(x+1)ĵ]\\cdot[2xî-3x^2ĵ]\\); (b) \\(g(x)=|\\sin xî-2xĵ+\\cos xk̂|\\).", "steps": ["Both outputs are scalars: a dot product in (a), a magnitude in (b).", "(a) Multiply corresponding components: f(x) = 2x²−3x²(x+1).", "Simplify f(x) = −3x³−x².", "Differentiate to get f′(x) = −9x²−2x.", "(b) Square and add the components: g(x) = √(sin²x+4x²+cos²x).", "Use sin²x+cos²x = 1, giving g(x) = √(1+4x²), positive everywhere.", "The chain rule gives g′(x) = 4x/√(1+4x²), for all real x."], "solution": "Both outputs are scalars: a dot product in (a), a magnitude in (b).\n(a) Multiply corresponding components: f(x) = 2x²−3x²(x+1).\nSimplify f(x) = −3x³−x².\nDifferentiate to get f′(x) = −9x²−2x.\n(b) Square and add the components: g(x) = √(sin²x+4x²+cos²x).\nUse sin²x+cos²x = 1, giving g(x) = √(1+4x²), positive everywhere.\nThe chain rule gives g′(x) = 4x/√(1+4x²), for all real x.", "answer": "(a) −9x²−2x; (b) 4x/√(1+4x²).", "progressiveSolution": true, "solutionOrigin": "SpaceBook learning enhancement", "sourceReferences": [{"page": 139, "jpg": "074_page_1.jpg", "verification": "all source subparts and derivative orders checked at enlarged resolution"}]}, {"id": "ex-5-2-q4", "qNo": "4", "question": "Find velocity, acceleration, speed and direction of motion at the indicated t: (a) \\(r⃗(t)=tî+t^2ĵ+2tk̂\\), t = 1; (b) \\(r⃗(t)=\\cos tî+\\sin tĵ+3tk̂\\), t = π/4; (c) \\(r⃗(t)=e^tî+e^{-t}ĵ+e^{2t}k̂\\), t = ln 2.", "steps": ["Use v⃗ = r⃗′, a⃗ = r⃗″, speed |v⃗| and direction v⃗/|v⃗| when velocity is nonzero.", "(a) v⃗(t) = î+2tĵ+2k̂; a⃗(t) = 2ĵ. At 1: v⃗ = î+2ĵ+2k̂, a⃗ = 2ĵ, speed √(1+4+4) = 3, direction (î+2ĵ+2k̂)/3.", "(b) v⃗(t) = −sin tî+cos tĵ+3k̂; a⃗(t) = −cos tî−sin tĵ.", "At π/4: v⃗ = −î/√2+ĵ/√2+3k̂, a⃗ = −î/√2−ĵ/√2, speed √10, direction (−î/√2+ĵ/√2+3k̂)/√10.", "(c) v⃗(t) = eᵗî−e⁻ᵗĵ+2e²ᵗk̂; a⃗(t) = eᵗî+e⁻ᵗĵ+4e²ᵗk̂.", "At ln 2, eᵗ = 2, e⁻ᵗ = 1/2, e²ᵗ = 4. Thus v⃗ = 2î−ĵ/2+8k̂ and a⃗ = 2î+ĵ/2+16k̂.", "The speed is √(4+1/4+64) = √273/2; direction is (4î−ĵ+16k̂)/√273. Each displayed direction has magnitude 1."], "solution": "Use v⃗ = r⃗′, a⃗ = r⃗″, speed |v⃗| and direction v⃗/|v⃗| when velocity is nonzero.\n(a) v⃗(t) = î+2tĵ+2k̂; a⃗(t) = 2ĵ. At 1: v⃗ = î+2ĵ+2k̂, a⃗ = 2ĵ, speed √(1+4+4) = 3, direction (î+2ĵ+2k̂)/3.\n(b) v⃗(t) = −sin tî+cos tĵ+3k̂; a⃗(t) = −cos tî−sin tĵ.\nAt π/4: v⃗ = −î/√2+ĵ/√2+3k̂, a⃗ = −î/√2−ĵ/√2, speed √10, direction (−î/√2+ĵ/√2+3k̂)/√10.\n(c) v⃗(t) = eᵗî−e⁻ᵗĵ+2e²ᵗk̂; a⃗(t) = eᵗî+e⁻ᵗĵ+4e²ᵗk̂.\nAt ln 2, eᵗ = 2, e⁻ᵗ = 1/2, e²ᵗ = 4. Thus v⃗ = 2î−ĵ/2+8k̂ and a⃗ = 2î+ĵ/2+16k̂.\nThe speed is √(4+1/4+64) = √273/2; direction is (4î−ĵ+16k̂)/√273. Each displayed direction has magnitude 1.", "answer": "(a) v⃗ = (1,2,2), a⃗ = (0,2,0), speed 3, direction (1,2,2)/3; (b) v⃗ = (−1/√2,1/√2,3), a⃗ = (−1/√2,−1/√2,0), speed √10, direction v⃗/√10; (c) v⃗ = (2,−1/2,8), a⃗ = (2,1/2,16), speed √273/2, direction (4,−1,16)/√273.", "progressiveSolution": true, "solutionOrigin": "SpaceBook learning enhancement", "sourceReferences": [{"page": 139, "jpg": "074_page_1.jpg", "verification": "all source subparts and derivative orders checked at enlarged resolution"}]}, {"id": "ex-5-2-q5", "qNo": "5", "question": "If F(t) is a differentiable vector function and F(t) ≠ 0, show \\(\\frac d{dt}\\frac{F⃗(t)}{|F⃗(t)|}=\\frac{F⃗′(t)}{|F⃗(t)|}-\\frac{[F⃗(t)\\cdot F⃗′(t)]F⃗(t)}{|F⃗(t)|^3}\\).", "steps": ["Put q(t) = |F⃗(t)|, which is positive because F⃗(t) ≠ 0.", "The squared norm is q² = F⃗·F⃗.", "Differentiate with the dot-product rule: 2qq′ = F⃗′·F⃗ + F⃗·F⃗′ = 2F⃗·F⃗′.", "Therefore q′ = (F⃗·F⃗′)/q.", "Differentiate the normalized vector F⃗/q with the scalar quotient rule: (F⃗/q)′ = F⃗′/q − q′F⃗/q².", "Substitute the norm derivative: (F⃗/q)′ = F⃗′/q − [(F⃗·F⃗′)F⃗]/q³, as required.", "The nonzero hypothesis permits every denominator. Differentiating the identity |F⃗/q|² = 1 also shows that this derivative is perpendicular to the unit direction vector."], "solution": "Put q(t) = |F⃗(t)|, which is positive because F⃗(t) ≠ 0.\nThe squared norm is q² = F⃗·F⃗.\nDifferentiate with the dot-product rule: 2qq′ = F⃗′·F⃗ + F⃗·F⃗′ = 2F⃗·F⃗′.\nTherefore q′ = (F⃗·F⃗′)/q.\nDifferentiate the normalized vector F⃗/q with the scalar quotient rule: (F⃗/q)′ = F⃗′/q − q′F⃗/q².\nSubstitute the norm derivative: (F⃗/q)′ = F⃗′/q − [(F⃗·F⃗′)F⃗]/q³, as required.\nThe nonzero hypothesis permits every denominator. Differentiating the identity |F⃗/q|² = 1 also shows that this derivative is perpendicular to the unit direction vector.", "answer": "The normalized vector derivative equals F⃗′/|F⃗| − [(F⃗·F⃗′)F⃗]/|F⃗|³.", "progressiveSolution": true, "solutionOrigin": "SpaceBook learning enhancement", "sourceReferences": [{"page": 139, "jpg": "074_page_1.jpg", "verification": "all source subparts and derivative orders checked at enlarged resolution"}]}];
