        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "i. The definite integral ∫ₐᵇf(x)dx presents the sum of the signed area between the graph of y = f(x) and the x-axis from x = a to x = b, where the area above the x-axis (peak) are counted positively and the area below the x-axis (valley) are counted negatively. This is shown in the Figure 6.6."
